\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Overview of the frozen general model and its plug-in modules. \textbf  {Left:} the frozen multi-task student (FastViT-SA24 hybrid, $\sim $8M parameters, 448\,px input) runs four general heads: semantic segmentation, inverse depth, lane, and a dense gate-corner head (stride 4, size level 56, top-K 8). Its weights are never modified. \textbf  {Center:} three small trainable modules have read-only access to the frozen stride-8 fused features. CornerRefiner refines each detected corner to sub-pixel accuracy in a second pass. CornerPeakHead (cpk3) confirms weak detections with a corner-peak heatmap. NearGateHead (ng2, threshold 0.6) detects near gates that fill the frame. Their outputs are merged with the core's initial detections (detection threshold 0.05). Two steps without learned parameters follow: global duplicate suppression (NMS, IoU 0.2) and a filter that drops boxes with a side under 14\,px. \textbf  {Right:} the filtered gate corners feed an unchanged third-party drone racing stack in Isaac Lab simulation, consisting of an EKF state estimator and a learned racing policy. Only the detector is swapped; the baseline is GateNet. Removing the modules restores the core bit-for-bit, so general metrics cannot get worse by construction. Hatching marks frozen parts, dashed orange borders mark trainable modules, and dotted borders mark steps without learned parameters.\relax }}{4}{figure.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:framework}{{1}{4}{Overview of the frozen general model and its plug-in modules. \textbf {Left:} the frozen multi-task student (FastViT-SA24 hybrid, $\sim $8M parameters, 448\,px input) runs four general heads: semantic segmentation, inverse depth, lane, and a dense gate-corner head (stride 4, size level 56, top-K 8). Its weights are never modified. \textbf {Center:} three small trainable modules have read-only access to the frozen stride-8 fused features. CornerRefiner refines each detected corner to sub-pixel accuracy in a second pass. CornerPeakHead (cpk3) confirms weak detections with a corner-peak heatmap. NearGateHead (ng2, threshold 0.6) detects near gates that fill the frame. Their outputs are merged with the core's initial detections (detection threshold 0.05). Two steps without learned parameters follow: global duplicate suppression (NMS, IoU 0.2) and a filter that drops boxes with a side under 14\,px. \textbf {Right:} the filtered gate corners feed an unchanged third-party drone racing stack in Isaac Lab simulation, consisting of an EKF state estimator and a learned racing policy. Only the detector is swapped; the baseline is GateNet. Removing the modules restores the core bit-for-bit, so general metrics cannot get worse by construction. Hatching marks frozen parts, dashed orange borders mark trainable modules, and dotted borders mark steps without learned parameters.\relax }{figure.caption.4}{}}
\newlabel{fig:framework@cref}{{[figure][1][]1}{[1][3][]4}}
